※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4540

※ A unit says what a number counts.  A truth value counts nothing and a code
※ point counts nothing, so there is nothing for a unit on one to say.  An array
※ is several of something, and the unit belongs to what it holds -- which is
※ where it is written: `u8 ¤meter⟦4⟧` is four lengths.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let flag: bool ¤meter = true
    0u6
